@0    = ~I was wondering, <CHARNAME>, what brought you to Amn? I have heard of your exploits in Baldur's Gate and I am curious as to why you came here.~
@1    = ~We were captured by a mage named Irenicus. And as for the reason why? I do not know. We escaped his dungeon, then we lost Imoen when she engaged him in a spell battle, which you know.~
@2    = ~After leaving Baldur's Gate, we were captured by a powerful wizard named Irenicus. We barely escaped his dungeon. Unfortunately I lost Imoen when she engaged him in spell battle.~
@3    = ~Ah yes the foul Cowled Wizards captured them. So you don't know why he captured you? Do you remember how he captured you?~
@4    = ~Not really. I remember we left Baldur's Gate, then I woke up in his dungeon a few days later. We lost Khalid and Dynaheir while we were there. From what Imoen told me, he was doing some kind of experiments on them. He did the same to me also and I don't know why. He never said why he wanted us and what these experiments were for.~
@5    = ~Experiments? How odd.~
@6    = ~You said when we met that you are hunting him, what do you know of this?~
@7    = ~What I know of him is that, he's a powerful mage that abuses magic for his own ends. I do not know why he would be performing experiments on you and your friends. I am curious, like yourself, in this matter.~
@8    = ~I do love being outdoors. I like adventuring in the city mind you, since human cities are new to me, but being outdoors is my home. What was it like being raised at Candlekeep?~
@9    = ~I enjoyed my time at Candlekeep. Gorion made sure I never stayed bored though. I would have to do a bunch of chores or study or sometimes both.~
@10   = ~It was rather dull and boring. I had to stay busy by doing stupid chores and study dusty old tomes. Boring!~
@11   = ~To tell the truth it was okay. After leaving Candlekeep I have found places and people that were very exciting compared to my home.~
@12   = ~I'd rather not talk about it.~
@13   = ~It sounds like you were busy as a child. It reminds me of my upbringing. I had to study scrolls and spell books for part of the day, then I would have to practice fighting the other half. It was a rare time for doing something on my own. Did Gorion allow you free time to do as you wish?~
@14   = ~Yes he did providing that I finished my chores and studying. If I did a good job, I would be allowed to go down by the ocean and swim or visit the nearby forest and play there.~
@15   = ~Sometimes he would. I had to make sure my chores and studying was up to his standards. On some weekends I was allowed to go swimming in the ocean or play in the forest.~
@16   = ~He did indeed. We should get going, Nina.~
@17   = ~Good. Sounds like Gorian wanted you to be close with nature. All intelligent beings should never forget their ties to nature.~
@18   = ~Doing work brings about character in a person. It's one of many things in life that would be considered a learning experience.~
@19   = ~Maybe so, but it was still dull and boring to me.~
@20   = ~I never thought of it that way. I'll remember this next time I do some hard labor.~
@21   = ~So you like to travel? It's good meeting new people and civilizations, a learning experience in itself. Well enough bantering, I have taken up enough of your time for now.~
@22   = ~The coming and goings of a city never cease to amaze me. Human civilization is full of the rich, the poor and those who look to make a fast coin. Very different from an elven civilization.~
@23   = ~How are elven cities different than humans?~
@24   = ~I always thought elven cities were similar to humans. They are not?~
@25   = ~That's nice to hear. Lets move along instead of chatting about such nonesense.~
@26   = ~Where I come from everyone is equal. We have some elves that are in the upper class, but that's because they have royal blood in them. We have no poor class like humans do. Our vendors are there too serve the greater whole of society, not make a quick coin for themselves.~
@27   = ~Sounds like a utopian society, Ninafer, but not realistic to humans. I guess things are different between elves and humans, especially in the out look of life.~
@28   = ~In a bad mood today? Very well if that's how you want to act I'll say no more about it.~
@29   = ~I know. It would seem that humans being short lived, they feel they must get a lot out of life while they can, which is unfortunate. They are always being rushed around. Do this, do that, it must be done now and quickly. Being in a rush, it , well its so alien to me. Being an elf makes me happy, I would not like to go through the struggles of a human or any other short lived race.~
@30   = ~Perhaps you could get more out of having a short life span than a long one. Ever think of that? We are adventurers after all.~
@31   = ~The problem with being longed lived is seeing friends and love one's pass on. Being short lived may not be so bad after all. Ever think of that?~
@32   = ~That very well could be, <CHARNAME>. Being an adventurer you could risk having your life end before its time. I see your point now. But we could also have a long prosperous life full of riches and grand tales to tell to your friends and family. Something to ponder on.~
@33   = ~To tell you the truth, it never crossed my mind. I am not very old in elven years, plus I have not had many friends outside of my elven life. None of my friends or family have died of old age either. Oh this is depressing me, <CHARNAME>!~
@34   = ~I am sorry, Ninafer. I did not mean to depress you, but this is a part of life you may have to experience sometime.~
@35   = ~Well get over it already. Life is short then you die.~
@36   = ~This is something you will have to face up to eventually, Ninafer. It's something we all must face up to.~
@37   = ~I know but it's something I do not look forward to. Do not worry though, I will be strong when it happens.~
@38   = ~Tactful and direct as always, <CHARNAME>. "Thanks" for being so blunt. I believe this conversation has ended.~
@39   = ~Face up to... when it comes I will be strong. Yes I will. Well we should get going.~
@40   = ~<CHARNAME>, should we not get some supplies? Last time I checked we were running low.~
@41   = ~Are they running low? I haven't been paying much attention to them.~
@42   = ~Oh great! Bring a woman within the sight of a few shops and she wants to spend all of the coins she has!~
@43   = ~I was just thinking of the same thing myself. We should get some more supplies the next time we are in sight of a shop.~
@44   = ~You haven't? Well you should, <CHARNAME>! Such carelessness could get us into trouble. What if we ran out of food far from the city or our supply of arrows dwindle down to nothing in a fight?~
@45   = ~You are right, Nina. I should be more careful with something that is important like supplies. We should pick up some stuff the next time we are in sight of a shop.~
@46   = ~Oh great we have mother with us. What next, tell me how to dress?~
@47   = ~My aren't we the little pig. You should watch that forked tongue of yours before a powerful mage turns you into a pig. I was thinking about getting supplies for the party. Yes, I will get some supplies for the party, one thing that is on top of the list is some slop for a pig I know.~
@48   = ~Great minds think alike aye, <CHARNAME>? We need some food for starters so we should pay a visit to the bakery and see if they have any elven bread. Yum, my favorite!~
@49   = ~Good. Since food is something we need immediately, we should get some of that first. Lets go find a bakery and see if they have some elven bread. Yum, my favorite!~
@50   = ~Quite the sense of humor you have there, <CHARNAME>. I am most likely your mother's age, being an elf after all. Since I now have the mother role in the party, we should get you some better clothes. We should visit the local playhouse and see if they have any jackass customs. I do believe it would fit you well.~
@51   = ~Tell me something about yourself, <CHARNAME>.~
@52   = ~Why do you want to know?~
@53   = ~There isn't much to tell. I was raised by monks in a library. I had an overbearing foster father who made me do stupid chores.~
@54   = ~I'm an adventurer.~
@55   = ~I'm a simple <PRO_RACE>, nothing more.~
@56   = ~Anything you wish to tell me. I would like to know a little bit about the <PRO_MANWOMAN> I follow.~
@57   = ~There really isn't much to tell. I was raised by monks in a library.~
@58   = ~I'm a simple adventurer. There really isn't much to tell.~
@59   = ~I'm a simple <PRO_RACE>, nothing more, nothing less.~
@60   = ~Raised in a library? I would imagine you learned about many things while there.~
@61   = ~I did. I learned a lot about history, one of my favorite topics.~
@62   = ~The old spell books always fascinated me. Well the books I had access to. I wasn't allowed to view the tomes that had powerful spells in them.~
@63   = ~I never paid much attention to any of it. All of that reading was boring to me.~
@64   = ~I rather enjoyed learning history. Knowledge of the past can be useful in the here and now or in the future.~
@65   = ~Interesting. My father had many ancient elven magical tomes. Some of them I couldn't read, they were written in ancient elvish. He even had a tome that was written in ancient draconic. He wouldn't allow me to read that tome though. Even if I could read ancient draconic, those spells were far too powerful for me.~
@66   = ~The quest of knowledge is never boring, not when it can help one out. You never know when the knowledge you learn can benefit you in a time of need.~
@67   = ~I believe you are more than a "simple" adventurer, <CHARNAME>. You thwarted the machinations of Sarevok, stopping the war that could have happened between Amn and Baldur's Gate. Plus many more stories about your travels along the Sword Coast.~
@68   = ~I did do that and more! I am the hero of the Sword Coast!~
@69   = ~I did have some help with my traveling companions, who happen to be good friends of mine.~
@70   = ~What I did was because of the possible rewards of wealth and fame, nothing more.~
@71   = ~What I did was what any honorable adventurer would do. I help out whenever I could, to those who needed it the most.~
@72   = ~Ah yes, the "hero" who's ego is larger than the Isle of Evermeet. I dare say, that you, <CHARNAME>, need a dose of a reality wake up call. I would imagine your future trials will give you such a wake up call.~
@73   = ~It's good to be surrounded by friends who can help you out and in turn, help them out when the situation presents itself. Friends should always be cherished, <CHARNAME>.~
@74   = ~That is quite the mercenary outlook you have, <CHARNAME>. The world is not all about acquiring wealth and satisfying your ego on how important you are. The world is more colorful than your black and white outlook after all.~
@75   = ~I am pleased to hear this, <CHARNAME>. A shame there are not that many adventurers that are like you, but perhaps the people you encounter can learn from your good deeds.~
@76   = ~A simple <PRO_RACE> I believe not. I have heard about you stopping the machinations of Sarevok, thus preventing the war that could have happened between Amn and Baldur's Gate. Plus many more stories about your travels along the Sword Coast.~
@77   = ~The sole purpose of what was done was because of the possible rewards of wealth and fame, nothing more.~
@78   = ~What I had done was what any honorable adventurer would do. I helped out whenever I could to those who needed it.~
@79   = ~We have the Tome of Magic that the priest wanted, <CHARNAME>. We should make haste and return it to him.~
@80   = ~This makes me happy, <CHARNAME>! I am so glad that you did this.~
@81   = ~What is it, <CHARNAME>? You have been silent as of late and have been looking at me quizzically. Have I done something wrong?~
@82   = ~Do you know Elhan? From the looks you gave to one another, it looked like you knew each other but kept it quiet.~
@83   = ~I was curious about the way you and Elhan looked at one another while we were at the elven camp. Did you know each other?~
@84   = ~Elhan? Yes I know him. He's a friend of my father if you must know.~
@85   = ~Strange that you two did not say anything to one another, not even a friendly hello.~
@86   = ~Is that so? Why didn't you say hello to him? Being a friend of your father, I would have thought that would be the polite thing to do.~
@87   = ~He's a family acquaintance, a friend of my father be it known. Why do you ask?~
@88   = ~I find it strange that you two did not say anything to one another, not even a friendly hello.~
@89   = ~A friend of my father he is but we have a strained relationship. This is something I prefer not to talk about any longer, <CHARNAME>. If you excuse me.~
@90   = ~NO!!! My city is under attack!~
@91   = ~Your city? Suldanessellar is your home? Explain yourself.~
@92   = ~Suldanessellar is your home? You better start explaining yourself Nina.~
@93   = ~Yes <CHARNAME> Suldanessellar was, is my home. It was...~
@94   = ~You never mentioned this before Nina, what is the meaning of this?~
@95   = ~Come on Nina tell me what is going on, you owe me.~
@96   = ~They, Elhan and the others, told me to join your party to watch over you. You were tainted by the Exile plus the blood of Bhaal you carry in your veins, they felt you may be a problem. They wanted me watch over you and report back to them in case you became another powerful evil being. But now... please, we have to help the elves defend the city! We have to find my father! <CHARNAME> you must help me, please!~
@97   = ~I will help you, Ninafer, but you need to get ahold of yourself. Stay focused on the task at hand and we will defeat them!~
@98   = ~Very well Nina, I will help you. You will owe me for doing this after what you said. Now try and stay focused on the task at hand and we will defeat them!~
@99   = ~I don't know if I should help you after this. I don't like being spied upon. Perhaps you need to start begging me for help.~
@100  = ~I am sorry for not telling you, but I was under orders. Please, please, <CHARNAME> help me. If not me then do it for the elves here.~
@101  = ~Much better Ninafer. I shall help you out but do pull yourself together.~
@102  = ~I think you need to work on your begging, Ninafer... bah, very well, I'll help you out. First thing you need to do is get it together. You're not going to get far in your current state of mind.~
@103  = ~Yes you're right, <CHARNAME>. I must stay focused on our enemies. I-I've never lost self control like that. Thank you. I don't know what I would do without you. Come, lets defeat these foul enemies!~
@104  = ~Bastard creature! How dare its vile presence grace my fair city! The traitor will surely pay for this outragous act!~
@105  = ~This is a new side of you, Ninafer, I like it.~
@106  = ~Nine remember what I said about staying focused. You're letting your emotions take control of your actions. We will get Irenicus but only if we keep ourselves in control of our actions.~
@107  = ~W-what? What do you mean?~
@108  = ~I have not seen you get like this before. You are so full of emotion and anger. It gives you an edge in battle I think.~
@109  = ~Umm nothing. Just forget I said anything.~
@110  = ~You of all people are always preaching about staying in control of your emotions and here you are losing control. Don't practice what you preach, Nina?~
@111  = ~You are right, <CHARNAME>, I'm getting unraveled again. This is something very personal to me. I have not been in a situation like this since I was a child. Come, we must get to the queen's palace.~
@112  = ~You are right, <CHARNAME>, I'm getting unraveled again. It may give you an edge in battle, briefly, but in the end you will get sloppy and get caught off guard. Come we must get to the queen's palace.~
@113  = ~Hmmm?. Ok. Come, we must get to the queen's palace.~
@114  = ~I've had enough of your evil ways! I'm leaving!~
@115  = ~(Gagging from the stench.) Ack! What a sickening smell! T-the people in here... what manner of beast did this to them?~
@116  = ~You! Another of that foul race of elves I see before me! How dare you walk openly amongst us!!~
@117  = ~Foul? I just bathed today.~
@118  = ~You know what I am talking about devil! Your evil blight must be wiped away by the sword!~
@119  = ~Another kook out of his cage. Go away.~
@120  = ~Typical arrogant elven pride. Being pushed aside as if I am below her. Your time will come evil one!~
@121  = ~(Nina rolls her eyes and moves away from him.)~
@122  = ~Well, hello there, fine looking sultry one. I like my women blond, curvy, and confident.~
@123  = ~Come home with me and I will show you a night of pure pleasure.~
@124  = ~Indeed? From my view, it would most likely be a night of dullness and despair.~
@125  = ~Dullness? No my sweet far from it! A fine specimen of femininity such as yourself, I would be your slave, doing your bidding for the whole night.~
@126  = ~You can do my bidding right now by leaving me alone.~
@127  = ~Oh no I couldn't do that. Come my sweet, shall I get a room for the two of us?~
@128  = ~Not to be rude, but I am losing my patience with you. The answer is no. No I do not want to spend the night with you, just leave me alone.~
@129  = ~You jest! Come now, stop playing hard to get my beautiful elf.~
@130  = ~Would you like me to turn you into a mouse and place you in a room full of cats? Or perhaps I can recite a spell that can make the blood boil inside your body, causing unbelievable pain. I know what I can do, cast a short levitation spell on you as you and float you over a lava pit, sound good to you?~
@131  = ~(He looks into his ale mug.) Oh my! Would you look at that! Time for a refill barkeep!~
@132  = ~Good boy, I knew you would see it my way eventually.~
@133  = ~My, what a pretty face. Do you use a special lotion to keep the skin soft and youthful?~
@134  = ~Lotions are not necessary. Elven skin is naturally soft and vibrant.~
@135  = ~That sure is a shiney sword you have lady. Can I play with it?~
@136  = ~No, you might poke your eye out.~
@137  = ~Wow! Yellow hair like the sun. Is your hair real? It looks fake to me.~
@138  = ~Of course it's real. Why don't you go play with some friends, child.~
@139  = ~You're no fun at all.~
@140  = ~You sure is pretty, elf lady. Are ya a serving wench at the Copper Coronet? Only the best looking ladies work there.~
@141  = ~I certainly do not work at the Copper Coronet nor would I lower myself to that unsavory level.~
@142  = ~Oh yer one of those stuck up nobles ain't ya?~
@143  = ~Begone child, I have matters that need my attention.~
@144  = ~It has been a while since I had fish. I will take one.~
@145  = ~Here ye go miss. Pleasure doin' business with ye.~
@146  = ~Oh that's just great, we're doing work for the lackies of Talos.~
@147  = ~Do not trust what she says if I were you, <CHARNAME>. If anything, I would question her intent.~
@148  = ~A good choice, <CHARNAME>. We do not fear you blood sucker, return to your grave while you are still able.~
@149  = ~Imoen will not fail undead beast, it shall be you who fails by our might!~
@150  = ~I would agree with your conclusion. It would appear a new leader has been put in charge and will do whatever they have to do, to accomplish their goals.~
@151  = ~Rude one are we not?~
@152  = ~Get out of the way!~
@153  = ~This doesn't look good if you ask me.~
@154  = ~Hmmm perhaps we should not be in here, <CHARNAME>.~
@155  = ~An ungrateful noble, how quaint.~
@156  = ~We are your superiors, it is your obligation to serve us.~
@157  = ~I do not like the idea of doing the deeds for Red Wizard trash, <CHARNAME>. But this is your group and I will do as you wish... to a point.~
@158  = ~Your scroll Edwin, I can feel the magical power that surges through it. Go ahead and read it.~
@159  = ~(Once again I suffer an interruption by those with their opinions. As if *I* would ask for it.) Of course I plan on reading it! Now be silent while I focus on the proper reading of the scroll.~
@160  = ~Your days of being a slaver are over, you foul beast!~
@161  = ~You will die by my blade, Irenicus, for your abuse to The Weave and the destruction of Suldanessellar! You bastard traitor Exile! DIE!~
@162  = ~I should have known Lehtinan was a filthy slaver. We must free the slaves and bring him to justice.~
@163  = ~Justice has been achieved.~
@164  = ~You can't just leave her like that, <CHARNAME>. It's horrible! I thought this was our quest, to save her!~
@165  = ~We must find a way to free Nalia, <CHARNAME>. We can not allow this to happen to her!~
@166  = ~You are an honorable man Keldorn, you will do what is right.~
@167  = ~Amazing! Such audacity these "nobles" have! We must find a way to free Nalia, <CHARNAME>.~
@168  = ~This cannot be allowed to continue.~
@169  = ~You look horrible, Jaheira. Do you need any help?~
@170  = ~No... (cough) no I do not need any help. I will manage j-just fine.~
@171  = ~Infidelity is the lowest of betrayals.~
@172  = ~Maria breaking this vow dishonors herself and all of those involved.~
@173  = ~This man makes my skin crawl, I hope our business with him is brief.~
@174  = ~Inadequate? If we are inadequate, why seek us for help?~
@175  = ~Silence foolish elf, I am speaking to, <CHARNAME>.~
@176  = ~Stealing from the priestess of Talos? I have no objections to this.~
@177  = ~I hope this cure works, Mazzy, I really do.~
@178  = ~Another problem arises, Nalia? Trouble seems to follow you where ever you go.~
@179  = ~This sounds like a good deal, <CHARNAME>. Go for it!~
@180  = ~Eh, sorry but no. You certainly not my type.~
@181  = ~<CHARNAME>, what... what was that? The transformation it was... was horrorifying. I need to... well nevermind. We will figure this out.~
@182  = ~A shame really, but I will not let anyone stand in our way from escaping this madhouse. This places makes my skin crawl.~
@183  = ~The traitor is dead, my mission is complete.~
@184  = ~Now we can inform the elves of this deed. Is there something wrong?~
@185  = ~Can this be true? Have I been damned even after all that I have done?~
@186  = ~Or is it you, <CHARNAME>, who have brought me here?~
@187  = ~The Cowled Wizards have warped the mind of this poor girl. What fiends they are.~
@188  = ~Yes we are awake, Irenicus. What do you mean it's as you predicted?~
@189  = ~We have hunted long and hard for you, Irenicus! Traitor! You will not live to see the end of this day!~
@190  = ~More like foolish enough to be caught with it on you.~
@191  = ~Betrayal at the hands a hireling who was suppose to help us. Unbelievable!~
@192  = ~Better to stay on friendly terms with the other guilds than become an enemy. A good idea if you ask me.~
@193  = ~So passes the great Amaunator. Peace at last.~
@194  = ~This king seems incompitent if you ask me, seeking our help when he has soldiers who could do the job.~
@195  = ~You are quite amusing child! You can not stop us. Stand down or this day may be your last!~
@196  = ~Bloody slaver scum!~
@197  = ~This is sick, <CHARNAME>! Watching poor animals forced to fight each other to the death is barbaric!~
@198  = ~You are wrong, abuser of magic! We shall never turn a comrade over to you!~
@199  = ~Quite a welcoming town, <CHARNAME>.~
@200  = ~<CHARNAME>! What are you doing? I can't believe you would commit such an evil act! I will not allow this!~
@201  = ~Veldrin, uh the gnomes would not stand a chance against us. Is this a good idea?~
@202  = ~(Ninafer smiles and says nothing.)~
@203  = ~I find looking like a drow revolting, <CHARNAME>. But if this is how we need to get to Irenicus then I will follow through with it.~
@204  = ~The illithids are revolting creatures. We must take them down quickly before they use their powers on us.~
@205  = ~This sounds like a a good plan. May we be victorious in this battle.~
@206  = ~<CHARNAME>, we need to act quickly on this, do not hesitate.~
@207  = ~What is she talking about?~
@208  = ~Not to trust you or any drow, you are correct on that.~
@209  = ~The people of Imnesvale do need our help but remember, <CHARNAME>, putting an end to Irenicus should be our first priority.~
@210  = ~The people of Imnesvale do need our help, but remember, <CHARNAME>, rescuing Imoen and putting an end to Spellhold should be our first priority.~
@211  = ~I disliked working for the Cowled Wizards from the beginning, now dispise them even more. They want your body to get inside this sphere? We can't support this, <CHARNAME>!~
@212  = ~The Cowled Wizards are known for lying and manipulating events to their favor. This situation looks like one of their well crafted lies.~
@213  = ~<CHARNAME>, it's bad enough you rescued this drow harlot, but to have her join with us? I really have my doubts about this course of action, but it's your group, do what you will.~
@214  = ~This is foul deed! May your heart be damned for this!~
@215  = ~(Nina sees Elhan then quickly looks away from him.)~
@216  = ~(Elhan finally notices Nina in the party, looks at her for a brief moment and then keeps on talking to you.)~
@217  = ~(Elhan finally notices Nina in the party, for a brief moment and then keeps on talking to you.)~
@218  = ~Nina, a loyal and noble friend who venerates Mystra, has accompanied you to bring justice to those who abuse The Weave stands before you.~
@219  = ~I hope you are ready for this, Ninafer. This battle is not going to be easy.~
@220  = ~Nina, Irenicus wants me, not you. I understand if you leave now.~
@221  = ~Ireincus is very powerful, Ninafer and none of us may not make it out. Are you sure you want a part of this?~
@222  = ~I am more then ready, <CHARNAME>. If I thought adventuring was going to be easy I would have never taken up the profession.~
@223  = ~I want to thank you for giving me a chance in your party. I have learned much from you. Now lets get this over with.~
@224  = ~No chance. Irenicus is the bane to The Weave and Mystra. It is my duty to bring him to justice, plus you are my friend and I will not leave you.~
@225  = ~I am sure, <CHARNAME>. As a defender of Mystra and your friend I will not leave your side.~
